  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 240 PM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nAs was mentioned in the short discussion, models show some uncertainty\nregarding how quickly the heaviest precipitation advances eastward\nby Thursday night. Some of the guidance shows the bulk of precipitation\nexiting far southeast counties Thursday afternoon, while others show\nheavy precipitation lingering through Thursday night. For now, will\nmaintain high POPs over the eastern portions of the Heartland and\nnorthwest Hill Country Thursday night and early Friday. While the\nthreat for heavy rainfall will come to an end by Friday, a weak trough\nwill reside over the area over the weekend, which will keep low to\nmedium (20 to 60%) rain chances lingering over the weekend. In addition,\nbelow normal temperatures are expected Friday through early next \nweek, with highs in the 70s through Monday. Overnight lows will be\nin the upper 50s and lower 60s.",
